<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">follow</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">follow</ansi> command lets you walk with someone. When they leave the
room, you go with them through the same exit.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">follow <name></ansi>  Start following someone in the room with you.
  <ansi fg="command">follow stop</ansi>    Stop following. <ansi fg="command">unfollow</ansi> does the same.
  <ansi fg="command">follow lose</ansi>    Make everyone who follows you stop. <ansi fg="command">lose</ansi> does the same.

<ansi fg="yellow">Parties</ansi>

  In a party you follow the party leader without this command. When the
  leader leaves a room, every member in that room goes too. You can still
  follow someone else, in your party or outside it.

<ansi fg="yellow">Following in the dark</ansi>

  You can only follow someone you see leave. Their light counts as well
  as yours: if they carry a light, you can follow them even when you
  carry none. Seeing their shape is enough.

  If you cannot see them go, because it is too dark or you are blinded,
  you stay where you are. A follow you started with this command ends
  then. Party members stay in the party, and follow the leader again
  next time they can see the leader leave.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help light</ansi>
